  "configuration_id": "config_039",
  "reason": "The current best configuration (config_037: multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) achieves 0.7062 accuracy. In RNA-only experiments, avgpool consistently outperformed transformer aggregation (0.5907 vs 0.5191 with pca_n2000), but this was tested without image features. config_039 changes only the aggregation from avgpool to transformer while keeping all other settings at their best-known values (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, weighted fusion, multiprofile). This isolates the effect of aggregation in the multimodal context where image features may interact differently with profile-level aggregation. If transformer aggregation helps here, it could push performance beyond 0.7062; if not, it confirms avgpool as the correct choice and directs remaining budget toward other design axes. This is a minimal single-variable extension of the strongest evidence, making it the most efficient use of the next experiment."
}

